                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>4. Open Alerts side panel</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Select the &apos;Watch&apos; dropdown arrow near the top right corner of the page (Toolbar)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>5. Add yourself to existing alerts/ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>Create your own alert</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>i) Select the y-axis </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#4e79a7' fontname='Tableau Medium' italic='true'>(Make sure it turns blue)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>ii) Select &apos;Create&apos; button in the Alerts tab</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>iii) Set the thresholds</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>Note: You can create Alerts on any other charts in Tableau, just make sure to always select the numeric axis first.</run>
